application framework","fork":false,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/netty/netty","forks_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/netty/netty/forks","keys_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/netty/netty/keys{/key_id}","collaborators_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/netty/netty/collaborators{/collaborator}","teams_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/netty/netty/teams","hooks_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/netty/netty/hooks","issue_events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/netty/netty/issues/events{/number}","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/netty/netty/events","assignees_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/netty/netty/assignees{/user}","branches_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/netty/netty/branches{/branch}","tags_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/netty/netty/tags","blobs_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/netty/netty/git/blobs{/sha}","git_tags_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/netty/netty/git/tags{/sha}","git_refs_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/netty/netty/git/refs{/sha}","trees_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/netty/netty/git/trees{/sha}","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/netty/netty/statuses/{sha}","languages_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/netty/netty/languages","stargazers_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/netty/netty/stargazers","contributors_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/netty/netty/contributors","subscribers_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/netty/netty/subscribers","subscription_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/netty/netty/subscription","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/netty/netty/commits{/sha}","git_commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/netty/netty/git/commits{/sha}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/netty/netty/comments{/number}","issue_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/netty/netty/issues/comments{/number}","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/netty/netty/contents/{+path}","compare_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/netty/netty/compare/{base}...{head}","merges_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/netty/netty/merges","archive_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/netty/netty/{archive_format}{/ref}","downloads_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/netty/netty/downloads","issues_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/netty/netty/issues{/number}","pulls_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/netty/netty/pulls{/number}","milestones_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/netty/netty/milestones{/number}","notifications_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/netty/netty/notifications{?since,all,participating}","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/netty/netty/labels{/name}","releases_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/netty/netty/releases{/id}","deployments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/netty/netty/deployments","created_at":"2010-11-09T09:22:21Z","updated_at":"2025-12-11T21:59:09Z","pushed_at":"2025-12-11T21:59:05Z","git_url":"git://github.com/netty/netty.git","ssh_url":"git@github.com:netty/netty.git","clone_url":"https://github.com/netty/netty.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/netty/netty","homepage":"http://netty.io","size":105564,"stargazers_count":34635,"watchers_count":34635,"language":"Java","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":true,"has_wiki":true,"has_pages":false,"has_discussions":true,"forks_count":16250,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":610,"license":{"key":"apache-2.0","name":"Apache License 2.0","spdx_id":"Apache-2.0","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/apache-2.0","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTI="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"topics":[],"visibility":"public","forks":16250,"open_issues":610,"watchers":34635,"default_branch":"4.2","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"body":"In an exception occurs in the \"inboundBufferUpdated\" Netty enters an infinite loop and nothing helps. Handling the exception in \"exceptionCaught\" and closing the context/pipeline/channel does not have any effect. Reading all bytes from the input buffer and/or clearing the buffer does not have any effect.\n\nThis issue is similar to:\nhttps://github.com/netty/netty/issues/1161\nand\nhttp://stackoverflow.com/questions/9592591/exceptioncaught-error-handling-write-back-response-causes-exception-and-infinite\n\nThe suggestion to close the channel in the exception handler did not work.\n\nA few questions and notes:\n- Why would you try to call the same handler again if it has already failed? Don't you think this can have side effects depending on what the handler does? What if always fails for some reason - this means we have potentially 100% CPU usage until the process is restarted!!!\n  What if the handler is designed to write to a database or to the file system and it does this each time it is called. Later it fails and it is run again!!! This can easily lead to adding millions of records to a database or writing filling the hard disk with data!!!\n- Most importantly closing the channel, reading all bytes from the input buffer (as suggested) by the other bug report had no effect!!!\n\nTo answer  Norman Maure's question about in what situation this can happen - it can happen, as in my case, when writing the received data into a file and the operation fails. I'm using ByteBuf.nioBuffer to get a ByteBuffer and write the data before calling ByteBuf.skipBytes to discard the written data (this is not a part of the next example).\n\nNote: Tried ctx.inboundByteBuffer().clear() instead of ctx.inboundByteBuffer().skipBytes(ctx.inboundByteBuffer().readableBytes()) with no difference.\n\nServer:\n\n```\npublic static void main(String[] args) throws InterruptedException {\n    ServerBootstrap b = new ServerBootstrap();\n    try {\n        b.group(new NioEventLoopGroup(), new NioEventLoopGroup())\n                .channel(NioServerSocketChannel.class)\n                .childHandler(new ChannelInitializer<SocketChannel>() {\n            @Override\n            public void initChannel(SocketChannel ch) throws Exception {\n                ChannelPipeline p = ch.pipeline();\n                p.addLast(\"handler\", new ChannelInboundByteHandlerAdapter() {\n                    private int _count;\n                    private int _countException;\n\n                    @Override\n                    protected void inboundBufferUpdated(ChannelHandlerContext ctx, ByteBuf in) throws Exception {\n                        _count++;\n                        System.out.println(\"'inboundBufferUpdated' called \" + _count + \" times\");\n                        Thread.sleep(1000);\n                        throw new Exception();                            \n                    }\n\n                    @Override\n                    public void exceptionCaught(ChannelHandlerContext ctx, Throwable cause) throws Exception {\n                        super.exceptionCaught(ctx, cause); //To change body of generated methods, choose Tools | Templates.\n                        _countException++;\n                        System.out.println(\"'exceptionCaught' called \" + _countException + \" times\");\n                        if (ctx.hasInboundByteBuffer()) {\n                            ctx.inboundByteBuffer().skipBytes(ctx.inboundByteBuffer().readableBytes());\n                        }\n                        ctx.close();\n                        ctx.pipeline().close();\n                        ctx.channel().close();\n                    }\n                });\n            }\n        });\n\n        // Bind and start to accept incoming connections.\n        b.bind(12345).sync().channel().closeFuture().sync();\n    } finally {\n        b.shutdown();\n    }\n}\n```\n\nClient:\n\n```\npublic static void main(String[] args) throws InterruptedException {\n    Bootstrap b = new Bootstrap();\n    try {\n        b.group(new OioEventLoopGroup())\n                .channel(OioSocketChannel.class)\n                .handler(new ChannelInitializer<SocketChannel>() {\n            @Override\n            protected void initChannel(SocketChannel ch) throws Exception {\n                ChannelPipeline p = ch.pipeline();\n                p.addLast(\"encoder\", new ObjectEncoder());\n            }\n        });\n        Channel channel = b.connect(\"localhost\", 12345).sync().channel();\n        channel.write(new byte[16]);\n    } finally {\n        b.shutdown();\n    }\n}\n```\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/netty/netty/issues/1205/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/netty/netty/issues/1205/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}},"event":"cross-referenced"}]